Why this file exists: the model card states plainly that "this release does not
include a Jinja-format chat template", and this pack's tokenizer_config.json has
no `chat_template` key. Without a template TabbyAPI serves /v1/completions only
and every /v1/chat/completions request fails.

Scope -- this covers `thinking_mode="chat"` with string content only:
  system / user / assistant turns, multi-turn, generation prompt.
It does NOT cover thinking mode (`<｜Assistant｜><think>` plus the
"Reasoning Effort: N" preamble), tool calls and their DSML encoding, images,
`latest_reminder`, or the `task`/`mask` quick-instruction fields. Those need
upstream's encoder or the deepseek-recipe toolkit; a request using them is
rejected below rather than silently mis-encoded.

Note that historical `reasoning_content` is deliberately dropped and replaced by
a bare `</think>`, which is what upstream's encoder does for past turns.

Verified against upstream by differential test: 18/18 conversation shapes match
`encode_messages(..., thinking_mode="chat")` exactly, plus published vector
tests/test_output_2.txt and the two chat-mode assertions in test_encoding.py.
The tokenizer sets add_bos_token=false, so this template emits BOS itself.
-#}
{%- if not add_generation_prompt is defined -%}{%- set add_generation_prompt = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{{- '<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- for message in messages -%}
    {%- if message['content'] is not string -%}
        {{- raise_exception('DeepSeek-V4.1 chat template: content must be a string; images and tool calls are not supported here -- see deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash encoding/encoding.py') -}}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if message['role'] == 'system' -%}
        {{- '<｜System｜>' + message['content'] -}}
    {%- elif message['role'] == 'user' -%}
        {{- '<｜User｜>' + message['content'] -}}
    {%- elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
        {{- '<｜Assistant｜></think>' + message['content'] + '<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
    {%- else -%}
        {{- raise_exception('DeepSeek-V4.1 chat template: unsupported role "' + message['role'] + '"; only system, user and assistant are encoded here') -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
    {{- '<｜Assistant｜></think>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
